    "summary": "This record describes a condensation reaction proceeding via nucleophilic aromatic substitution (SNAr) mechanism using DIPEA as base in DMA solvent. The reaction was performed in a Vapourtec R4+ flow reactor with a 10 mL reactor volume at 250°C with a 30-minute residence time and 1.0 mL/min flow rate, achieving 69% yield at 0.5 M concentration. The batch baseline was conducted at room temperature (25°C) for 30 minutes and achieved the same 69% yield. Flow chemistry enabled the use of significantly higher reaction temperature (250°C vs 25°C) while maintaining the same residence time and yield, suggesting improved reaction kinetics and process intensification through better heat transfer control in the continuous flow system.",
